From 17d650bba73533dd65cf6228355b19fd2c0e6207 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:48:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 247/280] WIP: ASoC: rockchip: rockchip_sai: Keep 32-bit slots
 when providing the clocks

Since the slot width follows the sample width in non-TDM mode, a 16-bit
stream from a clock-providing SAI uses 16-bit slots and a 32 fs frame.
The HDMI transmitter on RK3576 accepts only 64 fs frames from SAI6, so
16-bit audio on HDMI is silent. Kodi always sends IEC 61937 passthrough
(AC-3, DTS, TrueHD, DTS-HD MA) as S16_LE, so passthrough is silent while
LPCM still plays because Kodi sends it in a 32-bit container.

The codec that needed the narrower slots, NAU8822, is the clock provider
there, and the boards where the SAI provides the clocks worked with 32-bit
slots before and after that change. Keep the 32-bit slot width when the
SAI provides the clocks, as it did before, and follow the sample width
only when the codec provides them.

Fixes: 8a6391ec6693 ("ASoC: rockchip: rockchip_sai: Set slot width for non-TDM mode")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c
index 30b5e71d0937..c303732c652d 100644
--- a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c
@@ -629,9 +629,11 @@ static int rockchip_sai_hw_params(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 
 	regmap_update_bits(sai->regmap, reg, SAI_XCR_VDW_MASK | SAI_XCR_CSR_MASK, val);
 
-	if (!sai->is_tdm)
+	if (!sai->is_tdm) {
+		slot_width = sai->is_master_mode ? 32 : params_physical_width(params);
 		regmap_update_bits(sai->regmap, reg, SAI_XCR_SBW_MASK,
-				   SAI_XCR_SBW(params_physical_width(params)));
+				   SAI_XCR_SBW(slot_width));
+	}
 
 	regmap_read(sai->regmap, reg, &val);
 
